  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "About this dashboard: how to read it, terms explained",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How to read this page",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 1,
            "w": 24,
            "h": 8
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "html",
            "content": "<div style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:1.6\">\n<p>Each night is dated by the morning you woke up. Your watch estimates the stages from movement and heart rate,\nnot a sleep lab, so the pattern over weeks says more than any single night.</p>\n<p><b style=\"color:#5c7cfa\">Total sleep</b> is time asleep, all stages together.\n<b style=\"color:#3b5bdb\">Deep sleep</b> is the slow-wave stage, when you are hardest to wake; most of it comes in the first half\nof the night. <b style=\"color:#74c0fc\">Core sleep</b> is Apple's name for light sleep and usually fills most of the night.\n<b style=\"color:#9c36b5\">REM sleep</b> is the stage with the most vivid dreaming; its stretches get longer towards morning, so a\nshort night trims REM first. <b style=\"color:#f08c00\">Awake</b> counts brief wakings; everyone has some and most are never\nremembered.</p>\n<p>Some measures only come from newer watches or once a feature is switched on. A panel that says\n<i>not reported by your devices in this range</i> means no data, never zero.</p></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Last night",
      "description": "Total sleep, the most recent night recorded.",
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "healthlog-db"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "uid": "healthlog-db"
          },
          "rawQuery": true,
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawSql": "SELECT total_sleep_h AS \"Total sleep\" FROM sleep_nightly ORDER BY sleep_date DESC LIMIT 1",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "h",
          "decimals": 1,
          "noValue": "–",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
